1.3:
Your oils have a pleasing fragrance,
Your name is like purified oil;
Therefore the maidens love you.

2.9:
My beloved is like a gazelle or a young stag.
Behold, he is standing behind our wall;
He gazes through the windows;
He is peering through the lattice.

2.12:
The flowers have appeared in the land;
The time for pruning has arrived;
And the voice of the turtledove has been heard in our land.

3.1:
“On my bed night after night I sought him
Whom my soul loves;
I sought him but did not find him.

3.7:
Behold, it is the traveling couch of Solomon;
Sixty mighty men around it,
Of the mighty men of Israel.

4.9:
You have made my heart beat faster, my sister, my bride;
You have made my heart beat faster with a single glance of your eyes,
With a single strand of your necklace.

4.11:
Your lips, my bride, drip honey from the comb;
Honey and milk are under your tongue,
And the fragrance of your garments is like the fragrance of Lebanon.

5.1:
“I have come into my garden, my sister, my bride;
I have picked my myrrh along with my balsam.
I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey;
I have drunk my wine with my milk.
Eat, friends;
Drink and imbibe deeply, O lovers.”

5.7:
The watchmen who go about in the city found me,
They struck me and wounded me;
The guardsmen of the walls took away my shawl from me.

5.11:
His head is like gold, fine gold;
His locks are like clusters of dates
And black as a raven.

6.9:
She is the only one—my dove, my perfect one;
She is the only one of her mother;
She is the pure one of her who bore her.
The daughters saw her and called her blessed,
The queens and the concubines also, and they praised her, saying,

7.5:
Your head crowns you like Carmel,
And the flowing locks of your head are like purple threads;
The king is captivated by your tresses.

8.2:
I would lead you and bring you
Into the house of my mother, who used to teach me;
I would give you spiced wine to drink from the sweet wine of my pomegranates.

8.5:
“Who is this coming up from the wilderness
Leaning on her beloved?”
“Beneath the apple tree I awakened you;
There your mother was in labor with you;
There she was in labor and gave you birth.

8.11:
Solomon had a vineyard at Baal-hamon;
He gave the vineyard to caretakers.
Each one was to bring one thousand shekels of silver for its fruit.

8.12:
My very own vineyard is before me;
The thousand shekels are for you, Solomon,
And two hundred are for those who take care of its fruit.”
